From ec697404e66e0e13452b544510bee2034c607c33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:51:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(motion): a chord that grazes one piece's wall and
 leaves the area no longer clears

chord_clears read one midpoint when no edge crossed the chord. A chord
can run along a wall of one piece of the cutter-centre area, leave the
area at the end of that wall, and come back on a second piece on the
same line. On Milling-test.step with a default whole-model 2D Adaptive
the path fed along Y -32 from (-8.05, -32) to (32, -32) at every level,
0.94 mm into the part. The law now splits the chord at every vertex it
touches without a crossing and judges the midpoint of each piece.

Pinned by adaptive_pinch (a disc that pinches the band, Adaptive and
Offset, aligned and turned stock; the user's part through generate and
the program sim) and two chord_clear unit tests.

Fixes #1620

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
